% Generate `web/src/auth/ConnectClaudeModal.jsx`: the "Sign in with Claude"
% modal (OAuth) with an API-key fallback. OAuth uses the manual paste-code
% variant of the Claude Code flow (same as `claude setup-token`): ask the backend
% for an authorize URL, open it in the system browser (Electron routes external
% links out), the user approves and pastes back the code Claude shows, and the
% backend exchanges it for a token. The API-key path verifies the key with a live
% call before saving. On success the backend persists the credential to the local
% .env; here we just hand the returned status to `onConnected`. No inline styles —
% the class names below are the contract with web/src/styles.css.
%
% Default-export `ConnectClaudeModal({ onClose, onConnected, initialStatus })`.
% Imports: `useState`; `* as api from '../api.js'`; `ClaudeLogo, IconX, IconKey`
% from '../components/icons.jsx'. Module const `KEYS_URL =
% 'https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys'`.

State: `mode` ('claude' | 'key', init 'claude'), `authorizeUrl` ('' — set once the
OAuth flow has begun), `code`, `apiKey`, `busy` (false), `err` (null). Derive
`reauth = !!initialStatus?.authenticated`. Helper `openExternal(url)` =
`window.open(url, '_blank', 'noopener,noreferrer')`.

Three async handlers, each wrapping `setBusy(true); setErr(null)` / try /
`catch (e) { setErr(String(e.message || e)) }` / `finally { setBusy(false) }`:
- `beginOAuth`: `{ authorize_url } = await api.startOAuth()`, `setAuthorizeUrl`,
  `openExternal(authorize_url)`.
- `finishOAuth`: no-op if `!code.trim()`; else `onConnected?.(await
  api.finishOAuth(code.trim()))`.
- `connectKey`: no-op if `!apiKey.trim()`; else `onConnected?.(await
  api.connectApiKey(apiKey.trim()))`.

Layout: a `modal-overlay` (click closes) around a `modal auth-modal` (click stops
propagation).
- `auth-head`: an `auth-head-text` with an h3 (`reauth` ? 'Re-authenticate with
  Claude' : 'Connect your Anthropic account') and an `auth-sub` reading
  "OpenNolan's AI agent uses your own Anthropic account to build and edit your
  videos. Your credentials stay on this Mac." Then an `am-close` IconX button
  (title/aria-label "Close") calling `onClose`.
- `auth-body`, branching on `mode`:
  - 'claude': when no `authorizeUrl`, a `claude-btn claude-btn-lg` calling
    `beginOAuth` (disabled while `busy`) showing `<ClaudeLogo size={20} />` +
    (busy ? 'Opening…' : 'Sign in with Claude'). Once `authorizeUrl` is set, an
    `auth-step` with an `auth-steps` ol of two li — (1) "Approve access in the
    browser tab that just opened" followed by a parenthetical `linkish` button
    "reopen it" → `openExternal(authorizeUrl)`; (2) "Copy the code Claude shows
    you and paste it below." — then an `auth-input` text input (placeholder "Paste
    the code from Claude", value `code`, autoFocus, autoComplete off, spellCheck
    off, Enter submits `finishOAuth`) and a `claude-btn` calling `finishOAuth`
    (disabled while `busy` or empty code) showing `<ClaudeLogo size={16} />` +
    (busy ? 'Connecting…' : 'Connect'). Below either state, a `linkish auth-alt`
    button "Prefer to use an API key instead?" that clears `err` and switches to
    'key' mode.
  - 'key': an `auth-step` with an `auth-label` label ("Anthropic API key" + a
    `linkish` anchor to `KEYS_URL`, new tab, "Get a key ↗"), an `auth-input`
    password input (placeholder "sk-ant-…", value `apiKey`, autoFocus,
    autoComplete off, spellCheck off, Enter submits `connectKey`), a button
    calling `connectKey` (disabled while `busy` or empty key) showing `<IconKey
    size={15} />` + (busy ? 'Verifying…' : 'Verify & connect'), and a `linkish
    auth-alt` button "← Back to Sign in with Claude" that clears `err` and
    switches to 'claude' mode.
- After the branch, when `err` is set, an `auth-err` div "⚠ {err}".
